# Line length

- **Column limit: 140** (not 80/100/120).
- Source of truth: root `.clang-format` → `ColumnLimit: 140`.
- When writing or editing C++, keep statements on one line if they fit within 140 columns (tabs count toward display width per clang-format / editor tab width 4).
- Do not wrap early “for style”; only wrap when exceeding the limit or when clang-format would.
- Run `scripts/format_source.py` / clang-format for bulk reflow; do not mass-reformat unrelated files in drive-by edits.
